      "content": "I'll read the original test file and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture. The main readability issues are:\n1. The `data_samples()` entries are crammed into a single massive line\n2. Many unused data provider methods add noise (only `data_samples()` is used by `test_minusDays`)\n3. Many unused imports\n\nI'll write a clean version with only what's needed, with well-formatted data.Now I'll run the compile check.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file is cleaner and more understandable: unused data provider methods and imports were removed, and the `data_samples()` table is now formatted one entry per row with aligned columns, making the Julian-to-ISO date mappings easy to read at a glance."
